WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.770
I do cook every single day, you know, Drew.

2
00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.190
So I'm gonna show you how to make one

3
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.840
of my favorite Rossipes ever.
Rossipes!

4
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.463
This is split pea soup with a little twist.

5
00:00:07.463 --> 00:00:08.296
Mm.

6
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.660
It's a Rossipe. Ta-da.
(audience applauds)

7
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.210
All right, so you know I cook every day,

8
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.870
and I like to sort of tip things on their head

9
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.250
and make my version of them.

10
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.480
This actually came out of a pandemic.

11
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.100
There was a day I wanted to cook something,

12
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.610
it was a weekend, and I had like nothing in the house.

13
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:27.960
And so I thought, what do I have?

14
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.840
And I actually had some split peas and some chorizo.

15
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.690
What? What do you do with that?

16
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.010
Well, I'm gonna turn this on its head.

17
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.230
I have some onions and carrots sweating

18
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.860
in a little bit of olive oil.

19
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.220
We're gonna do a little salt and pepper in here.

20
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.310
And if you're open to a little heat,

21
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.197
I like to do some red pepper.

22
00:00:46.197 --> 00:00:48.310 line:15%
And you can just, crushed red pepper, you know?

23
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.880 line:15%
Yes, please.
Do as much as you want.

24
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.453 line:15%
I'm old. My palate is dull.

25
00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.210 line:15%
Once those are sort of translucent,

26
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.190 line:15%
we're gonna add two cloves of garlic.

27
00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.630
You just wanna brown it slightly.

28
00:00:58.630 --> 00:00:59.463
Mm-hmm.

29
00:00:59.463 --> 00:01:01.950 line:15%
And then I have about eight cups of chicken stock.

30
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.810 line:15%
You can use veggie stock if you want to.

31
00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.640 line:15%
Now we're gonna add some herbs.

32
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.940 line:15%
I do some dried oregano in here.

33
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.110 line:15%
I put one bay leaf, which we're gonna get out later.

34
00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.050 line:15%
Here's some fresh thyme.

35
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.920 line:15%
You can use dried, too, if you want.

36
00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.720 line:15%
And now is when my split pea soup goes a little crazy.

37
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.553
Hmm.

38
00:01:20.553 --> 00:01:21.903
We're gonna put smoked paprika in there.

39
00:01:21.903 --> 00:01:22.930
(dish clanging)

40
00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.800
Right? Why?

41
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.840
Because I'm going to take this dried chorizo,

42
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.610
it's a hard chorizo sausage, right?

43
00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.930
In here are spices like paprika, chili powder. Yummy, yummy.

44
00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.240
And while the soup cooks and boils,

45
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.400
all those spices are gonna render into the broth,

46
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.550
seasoning our entire broth.

47
00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:44.410
Then you take your split peas

48
00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.230
and put them into this broth as well.

49
00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:49.860
How long does this cook now?

50
00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.900
Because I think some people are unintimidated

51
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.200
and some people are like, how long do I cook the lentils?

52
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.430
I would say a couple hours you're gonna want this

53
00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.340
to cook down.
Okay.

54
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.700
So now is when we're gonna take our tongs

55
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.840 line:15%
and grab this chorizo and take it out of here.

56
00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.490 line:15%
Oh, my gosh, Ross.

57
00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:08.323 line:15%
Can you smell it?

58
00:02:08.323 --> 00:02:09.940 line:15%
This looks incredible.

59
00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.170
So set this aside.

60
00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.740
We're actually going to let this cool, the chorizo.

61
00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.790
And once it has cooled, we're gonna dice it.

62
00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:16.900
So you'll notice right now,

63
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.280
our split pea is a little chunkified still,

64
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.740 line:15%
and you can serve it like this.

65
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.240 line:15%
But I thought it'd be fun to get this bad boy out.

66
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.251 line:15%
You guys are ever work with an immersion blender?

67
00:02:25.251 --> 00:02:26.180
(blender whirs)

68
00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:27.940
Oh, yeah. Hey.

69
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.640
This is very dangerous
(audience laughs)

70
00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.199
and fun, but you immerse it

71
00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:32.032
into-
Oh, shoot.

72
00:02:32.032 --> 00:02:32.865
Yeah, be careful.

73
00:02:32.865 --> 00:02:33.890
I was gonna say the best thing to do

74
00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.490
is to stick it in the soup,

75
00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:37.720
and then turn it on.
(audience laughs)

76
00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.970
Yes, you don't wanna turn it on

77
00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.490
and then put it into the soup

78
00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:42.300
'cause it'll all go all over the kitchen.

79
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.410
Yes, exactly. Ugh.

80
00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.290
Oh, shoot, I forgot to take the bay leaf out.

81
00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.300
Ah, man.

82
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.200
Uh-oh.

83
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.990
Well, okay. So take the bay leaf out.

84
00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.300
That's very important.
(audience laughs)

85
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.570
See, what's fun about the kitchen

86
00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.040
is that it doesn't matter if you mess up

87
00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.160
because no one's watching unless you're on television.

88
00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.456
So hi.
Yes, exactly.

89
00:02:56.456 --> 00:02:57.580
(Drew and audience laughing)

90
00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.770
Okay, so let's scoop up a little bowl here.

91
00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.110
Mm-hmm.
Okay.

92
00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.790
All right, we have our soup here.

93
00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.100
Now remember that chorizo?

94
00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.230
I can never forget it.

95
00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:07.690
Okay, we're gonna,
(audience laughs)

96
00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.650
we're gonna garnish our soup with it,

97
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.460
because just like when you cook it with the ham hock

98
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.620
